{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> Now Moses asked what name he would say to Israel of His names, for by the name El Shaddai signs are not performed, only by the honored name. And Rabbi Yeshuah said that there was a tradition among Israel from their fathers, that the savior of Israel would reveal a new name that had not been heard. And when he saw \"I am YHWH who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldeans\" (Genesis 15:7), he explained it as words of Moses, and he was not correct, for behold at the beginning of the Torah in the portion of Genesis, the honored name is not written, only Elohim, until \"to make,\" and from there onward it is written YHWH Elohim, and from the birth of Cain onward the name alone is written. And never in the words of Moses is the name Elohim found, only the honored name, except in one place, because Pharaoh said \"Entreat YHWH, and let there be enough of the thunder of Elohim\" (below 9:28) [n: cited by Ibn Ezra as verse 25, but the correct verse number is 28; the Hebrew text reads ט כה], then Moses said, because of YHWH Elohim (there 9:30), and the like is not found again in all the Torah:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's Hebrew cites the Pharaoh verse as ט כה (9:25) but the words quoted match 9:28 (Exodus 9:28); the reference is given as 'below' meaning later in Exodus. The phrase ולא ימצא עוד בכל התורה ככה closes the comment with no explicit continuation marker."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:20.519454453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}